// ============================================================================
// Regression fixture - valid/memory_tests - MemoryContract
//
// The Phase 1 memory-domain contract skeleton (docs/memory-domains.md §5.1,
// §9 Phase 1): a `memory` declaration parses, the compiler validates its
// contract - required acquire/release, the optional reset/exhausted/
// onCollect, each public, each with its exact signature - and the program
// still runs. The declaration under test lives in this case's helper module
// (FrameArena.zl, sibling of the entry): one primary type per file, imported
// by name.
//
// The invalid halves live in tests/zl/invalid/memory_tests/, one fixture per
// rule (MemoryMissingRelease, MemoryContractSignature, MemoryContractPrivate,
// MemoryContractDuplicate, MemoryPublicHelper, MemoryPublicField,
// MemoryConstructor, MemoryStaticMember, MemoryConstructRefused,
// MemoryExtendsRefused, MalformedMemoryDecl).
// ============================================================================

import FrameArena

class MemoryContract {
    func main(): void {
        // The declaration is checked but inert: no allocation exists yet, so
        // there is no value of FrameArena to hold - only the proof that the
        // contract above typechecks, which is this program running at all.
        log("memory contract ok")
    }
}
